WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:04.838
I joined the Army back in 1995
when I was 17 years old.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:07.549
If you remember, in 1995,
Oklahoma City

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:10.844
experienced a terrorist bombing
and it inspired me

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:13.346
to do something to help
my community.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.101
My name is Marnie Robbins-
Hoffman.

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:20.979
I was in the Connecticut Army
National Guard.

00:00:20.979 --> 00:00:23.523
I'm currently assigned
as a patrol sergeant

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.483
at the Yale Police Department.

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:28.403
Having the Yale
veterans community behind us

00:00:28.403 --> 00:00:31.281
and with us
walking with us is helpful

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:33.533
because it is a group of people
that have been through

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.536
some of the same challenges
that we've all been through.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.038
Veterans Day
has a great meaning to me.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:40.915
This is a day
for us to remember everything

00:00:40.915 --> 00:00:43.042
that we've done,
everything that we've achieved,

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:44.502
and to remember the friendships

00:00:44.502 --> 00:00:46.629
and the camaraderie
that we've made throughout

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:48.256
our time in the military.

00:00:48.256 --> 00:00:50.675
Most of all, it's a day of
deep appreciation

00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:53.511
for everybody that's ever worn
a uniform.

